cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use runboard in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "runboard: a local dashboard and working environment for machine-learning training runs"
abstract: >-
  runboard starts, queues, follows and compares training runs on this computer, Kaggle, a machine over SSH or a
  SLURM cluster, and keeps every result as a readable file in the project. Optionally, it runs pre-registered
  experiments: hypotheses decided with confidence intervals, a locked plan with recorded deviations, and paper
  output.
authors:
  - family-names: Toker
    given-names: Alperen
version: 0.4.5
date-released: 2026-11-11
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/alperentoker/runboard-ml"
url: "https://alperentoker.github.io/runboard-ml/"
keywords:
  - machine learning
  - experiment management
  - training dashboard
  - kaggle
  - slurm
  - pre-registration
  - reproducibility
